  "human_summary": "On 20 December 2024, a road crash occurred at the Nila Market intersection on the 300-feet road in Purbachal, Bangladesh, killing BUET student Muhtasim Masud (22) and critically injuring his two friends, Amit Saha and Mehedi Hasan [ev_850f0b4bcf2418e4, ev_f6979130e8086261]. According to The Business Standard, the three youths were on a stationary motorcycle talking to police when a car driven by Mubin crashed into them; Mubin is described as driving recklessly [ev_3cb89b4791adcc04]. A case was filed by the victim's father under the Road Transport Act 2018, and a Narayanganj court sent the three accused to jail [ev_23e903df4479a2d7, ev_850f0b4bcf2418e4]. Casualty figures are consistent across the available reports. The exact crash coordinates are not supplied; the location is representative of the Purbachal area.",
